		<item>
		<title>New analysis reveals £43bn annual open banking opportunity for the UK economy</title>
		<link>https://www.openbanking.org.uk/news/new-analysis-reveals-43bn-annual-open-banking-opportunity-for-the-uk-economy/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Patrick Cannon]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 16 Mar 2026 10:48:12 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Data highlights]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Press Releases]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Report]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Analysis]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Banking]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Data]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.openbanking.qa/?p=26038</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Open banking has already delivered £8.3bn to the UK economy, with significant headroom for growth as adoption expands London, UK: Open banking could unlock significant economic benefit for the UK as adoption expands, according to new independent economic analysis commissioned by Open Banking Limited (OBL) and with analysis completed by EY to help OBL quantify, [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/news/new-analysis-reveals-43bn-annual-open-banking-opportunity-for-the-uk-economy/">New analysis reveals £43bn annual open banking opportunity for the UK economy</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.openbanking.org.uk">Open Banking</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<div style="height:16px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" style="font-size:27px">Open banking has already delivered £8.3bn to the UK economy, with significant headroom for growth as adoption expands</h2>



<div style="height:16px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow" style="flex-basis:70%">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>London, UK: </strong>Open banking could unlock significant economic benefit for the UK as adoption expands, according to new independent economic analysis commissioned by Open Banking Limited (OBL) and with analysis completed by EY to help OBL quantify, for the first time, the potential impact of open banking in terms of the value delivered for consumers, businesses and the wider economy.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This analysis finds that open banking has already delivered an estimated £8.3bn in cumulative benefit to date, based on current levels of adoption. Looking ahead, annual economic benefits could reach £7.4bn after five years as adoption continues to scale. At full maturity and adoption, the long-term annual opportunity across the UK economy could be significantly larger, reaching up to £43bn per year.</p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><a href="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking-the-everyday-value-growth-opportunity-open-banking-UK.pdf" target="_blank" rel=" noreferrer noopener"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="955" height="537" src="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail.png" alt="" class="wp-image-26040" srcset="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail.png 955w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-300x169.png 300w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-768x432.png 768w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-375x211.png 375w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-512x288.png 512w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-100x56.png 100w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-78x44.png 78w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-43x24.png 43w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-28x16.png 28w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-70x39.png 70w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-82x46.png 82w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-175x98.png 175w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-345x194.png 345w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 955px) 100vw, 955px" /></a></figure>



<div style="height:9px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



<div class="wp-block-buttons alignwide is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-fe48e5de wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link has-magenta-background-color has-background wp-element-button" href="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking-the-everyday-value-growth-opportunity-open-banking-UK.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong>Read the analysis</strong></a></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The findings demonstrate the growing role of open banking in driving economic growth, highlighting its importance as part of the UK’s financial infrastructure and the significant headroom for future growth. The analysis shows that open banking is already delivering measurable economic value, with £8.3bn in benefit realised to date based on current adoption levels.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The modelling identifies how cumulative adoption across payments, savings, lending and cloud accounting could generate economy‑wide benefits as millions of everyday financial decisions become cheaper, faster and more efficient over time. Open banking is the consent-based data sharing of current account data with trusted third parties, and this research highlights a number of benefits that open banking facilitates, such as:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Improved financial management for consumers &#8211; enabling people to save more and reduce unnecessary living costs.</li>



<li>Productivity gains for businesses through automation &#8211; lower transaction costs and reduced administrative burden.</li>



<li>Increased investment and growth &#8211; as better use of data and payments improves access to finance and directs capital towards more productive uses.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For SMEs, reducing the cost of administration can release more time for SMEs to focus on growth, not paperwork &#8211; driving the development of new, innovative products and services generating an estimated annual GDP uplift of £2.3bn within the next five years.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For consumers, open banking-powered tools could help them manage and save money more effectively, and access fairer finance, supporting increased economic activity. This is estimated to deliver an annual boost to UK GDP of £2.5bn within the next five years.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Beyond direct consumer and business benefits, the analysis highlights that open banking can act as a material driver of economic growth, supporting higher productivity, increased investment, and more efficient allocation of capital.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Henk Van Hulle, CEO of Open Banking Limited, said:</strong></p>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">“<em>Open banking has already played a vital role in society with over 17.5 million user connections, and these findings show that there is an even greater opportunity ahead now that open banking has reached a key point of maturity.”</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>“By helping consumers manage their money better and enabling businesses to operate more efficiently, open banking is already contributing meaningfully to economic growth, a key component of the Government’s wider growth mission.</em></p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="393" height="393" src="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Henk-2.png" alt="" class="wp-image-26041" srcset="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Henk-2.png 393w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Henk-2-300x300.png 300w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Henk-2-150x150.png 150w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Henk-2-375x375.png 375w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Henk-2-100x100.png 100w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Henk-2-78x78.png 78w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Henk-2-43x43.png 43w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Henk-2-28x28.png 28w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Henk-2-70x70.png 70w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Henk-2-46x46.png 46w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Henk-2-194x194.png 194w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 393px) 100vw, 393px" /></figure>
</div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em><em>“As the UK looks to strengthen productivity, competitiveness and innovation across financial services, this analysis underlines the important role open banking can play in supporting those ambitions, while laying the foundations for the next phase of development.”</em></em></p>



<div style="height:100px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Thomas Bull, Head of FinTech Growth at EY, said:</strong></p>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="393" height="393" src="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Tom-Bull.png" alt="" class="wp-image-26042" srcset="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Tom-Bull.png 393w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Tom-Bull-300x300.png 300w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Tom-Bull-150x150.png 150w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Tom-Bull-375x375.png 375w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Tom-Bull-100x100.png 100w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Tom-Bull-78x78.png 78w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Tom-Bull-43x43.png 43w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Tom-Bull-28x28.png 28w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Tom-Bull-70x70.png 70w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Tom-Bull-46x46.png 46w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Tom-Bull-194x194.png 194w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 393px) 100vw, 393px" /></figure>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>“Open banking is already delivering real and substantial value across the UK, with significant further growth potential as adoption continues to scale. It is changing how people and businesses manage everyday financial activity from making and receiving payments, to managing cash flow, reducing administrative burden and making more informed decisions in real time. The report shows that these improvements to routine, everyday interactions are already unlocking meaningful benefits for consumers and businesses alike, and that their impact grows as adoption deepens.</em></p>
</div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>“Looking ahead, continued collaboration between industry, regulators and government will be critical to building on this momentum, scaling the existing ecosystem and supporting the transition towards open finance, enabling broader, fairer access to financial services across the UK.”</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Read the full report:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Stay informed. Stay secure. Explore the data and insights driving the future of open banking.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a id="_msocom_3"></a></p>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"></div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><a href="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking-the-everyday-value-growth-opportunity-open-banking-UK.pdf"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="955" height="537" src="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail.png" alt="" class="wp-image-26040" srcset="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail.png 955w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-300x169.png 300w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-768x432.png 768w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-375x211.png 375w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-512x288.png 512w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-100x56.png 100w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-78x44.png 78w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-43x24.png 43w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-28x16.png 28w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-70x39.png 70w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-82x46.png 82w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-175x98.png 175w, https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking_The_Everyday_Thumbnail-345x194.png 345w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 955px) 100vw, 955px" /></a></figure>



<div style="height:9px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



<div class="wp-block-buttons alignwide is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-fe48e5de wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link has-magenta-background-color has-background has-text-align-center wp-element-button" href="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/Unlocking-the-everyday-value-growth-opportunity-open-banking-UK.pdf"><strong>Download the report</strong></a></div>
</div>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"></div>
</div>


<div class="taxonomy-post_tag wp-block-post-terms"><span class="wp-block-post-terms__prefix">Tags</span><a href="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/news/tag/analysis/" rel="tag">Analysis</a><span class="wp-block-post-terms__separator">, </span><a href="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/news/tag/banking/" rel="tag">Banking</a><span class="wp-block-post-terms__separator">, </span><a href="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/news/tag/data/" rel="tag">Data</a><span class="wp-block-post-terms__separator">, </span><a href="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/news/tag/report/" rel="tag">Report</a></div>


<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><u>Notes to editors</u></strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">*More than 17.51 million user connections are live across the UK, supported by a growing ecosystem of 145 authorised third-party providers, delivering services used daily by consumers, small businesses, and public bodies. In January 2026 the number of open banking payments rose 4.3% month on month to 36.04 million. <br><em>Source: </em><a href="https://www.openbanking.org.uk/api-performance/"><em>API performance stats &#8211; Open Banking</em></a></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>About the economic analysis:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This economic analysis presents an impact assessment of Open Banking in the UK as of December 2025. It explores how emerging technologies and regulatory developments are unlocking the next phase of Open Banking tools, with a focus on the tangible benefits delivered to consumers, small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs), and the wider economy.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The modelling reflects conservative adoption assumptions and publicly available data, designed to provide a robust, economy-wide view of how value scales as open banking matures.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">WA Communications, <a href="mailto:openbanking@wacomms.co.uk">openbanking@wacomms.co.uk</a>&nbsp;</p>



